# Paths worth a second look before they reach main. NOT a gate: see the warning below.
#
#   .github/workflows/  is the Gate itself. A Run that weakened claude-review.yml or ci.yml
#                       would face no reviewer on the pull request after it.
#   db/migrations/      is the least reversible thing here. A bad schema change cannot be
#                       undone by reverting a commit.
#   CODEOWNERS          is this rule. It should not be editable by the thing it constrains.
#
# This file does not stop anything, and it is written down here so that nobody reads it as
# though it does.
#
# Two reasons, either of which would be enough. The branch ruleset's only bypass actor is the
# repository admin role, always, and Runs act as Jack, who holds it. And the review this file
# asks for cannot be given: GitHub does not let anyone approve their own pull request, and a
# Run's pull request is authored by Jack, so his code-owner approval on it is impossible
# rather than merely missing. #147 changed a workflow and merged without him seeing it.
#
# Making it real would mean the Runs having a GitHub identity of their own. That was
# considered on 2026-09-18 and deliberately not done: this is a single-player repo and every
# commit in it is Jack's either way. What the file is for now is flagging: a pull request
# touching one of these paths should say so plainly, because nothing else will.

/.github/workflows/   @fieldjw96
/db/migrations/       @fieldjw96
/.github/CODEOWNERS   @fieldjw96
